course: dictionary
lesson: 13738
title: Done on purpose
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Intentional means done on purpose. If you chose to do something and meant it to happen, it was intentional. Look for clue words such as on purpose, deliberately, or meant to.
explain: «Mia wrote a note on purpose to tell her brother the news.» Writing the note was intentional, because Mia meant to do it. «Sam tripped over his bag and spilled his drink by accident.» That was not intentional, because he did not mean to spill it.
explain: A quick check: ask, did the person mean to do it? If yes, intentional fits. Put «on purpose» into the sentence in place of the hard word. If it still makes sense, you have found the meaning.
fact: Intentional means done on purpose, deliberately, not by accident.
fact: «An intentional push» is a choice, but «an accidental bump» is not.
fact: In sport, an intentional foul gets a bigger punishment than an accident.
fact: In law and fairness, what a person intended can change how wrong an action is.
fact: Intentional can also be good, like «intentional kindness», which means being kind on purpose.
exercise: «The teacher made an intentional choice to sit the twins apart.» What does intentional mean here? | Done at night | Done by accident | *Done on purpose | Done very slowly
exercise: «Ben dropped his pencil by accident.» Was this intentional? | Yes, because pencils are small | Yes, he meant to drop it | Not sure, it could be either | *No, he did not mean to
exercise: Which one is intentional kindness? | *Ruby made a card and gave it to a sad friend on purpose | Ruby hid the sweets by mistake, then forgot where | Ruby knocked over a bin and said sorry | Ruby tripped on the stairs
test: «The fox made an intentional move to hide behind the tree.» What does intentional mean? | *On purpose | By chance | Quietly | Very fast
test: «The glass broke, but Tom did not break it on purpose.» Was the breaking intentional? | Yes, glass always breaks on purpose | *No, it was an accident | Yes, Tom planned it | It is impossible to say
exam: Which word means done on purpose? | careless | accidental | *intentional | sudden
